{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits","id":10053,"title":"Creative Uses for Embeds & Exploits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T15:59:49-08:00","id":10053,"title":"Creative Uses for Embeds & Exploits","content":"Exactly what it says on the label, my friends. Post what comes to mind<br /> <br /> For me, I'm planning to use In My Pocket to be a drug dealer; nobody knows what I have hidden inside my hobo coat, so I'm gonna pull drugs out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T23:44:49-08:00","id":10244,"title":"","content":"This is a bit loose of the theme of this thread, but a thought occured to me...<br /> <br /> If you're in a game where you need to get into a Facility and need a way to draw off a Guardian, what if you filled a gadget with Aether then blew the thing outside the facility? It'd draw the attention of all nearby angels, perhaps to a confrontation with some cultists... leaving your Demons a great opportunity to sneak into the facility and acquire whatever you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:43:19-08:00","id":10363,"title":"","content":"A Gadget with the Interference Embed worked in, perhaps? Like an Aether grenade? Keen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:01:58-08:00","id":10576,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this counts as &quot;creative use&quot;, but there are a number of ways to give Knockout Punch a ~90% success rate. Even against tremendously powerful enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>Knockout Punch + Momentum + Just Bruised</b>: Your first combat action attack all out, abandoning defense. When the attacked enemy retaliates use Momentum to gain extra dice and Just Bruised to reduce all damage to 1. Respond next action with Knockout Punch, augmented with willpower and Momentum. The 4 - 8 bonus dice will probably be enough to well surpass an enemies defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Knockout Punch + Ambush</b>: With a few minutes a demon can set up a basically irresistible ambush, denying all enemies their first action and defense. Toss in Hesitation or Strike first and the Demon could potentially drop two enemies (totally ignoring defense for the first) before the rest get an opportunity to act. Put in perspective, he could drop an enemy with Defense 15 and 10/10 soak 95% of the time on action one. Diversion also works as a less effective, more flexible substitute for Ambush. As does Lost in the Crowd.<br /> <br /> <b>Knockout Punch + Shift Consequence</b>: Not 100% certain if this works, but if it does it's another doozy. Action 1 use knockout punch on someone who can't, or isn't trying to, defend against it. Action 2, use Shift Consequence to move the effect to the desired target. As the roll is Resisted, a Demon can fairly reliably make this happen giving an upwards of 80% success rate or higher against most foes. (Most foes here meaning enemies with Resistance 6 or less).<br /> <br /> <b>Knockout Punch + Demon House</b>: Fuse with a house, use any Embed you want on the inhabitants. Don't really know how I'd adjudicate Brawl attacks while in building form as the ST, but I expect it'd be pretty easy to explain how the enemy is caught unaware. End result, everyone in the house (assuming it's not too crowded) to sleep.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> As a related note, I've changed Knockout Punch to being reflexive, activated when an attack connects, forgoing all damage for a Dexterity + Brawl vs Resolve + Supernatural Advantage roll. It remains strong, but not as goofy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:05:13-08:00","id":10579,"title":"","content":"Wow, those are really clever. I love the idea of doors or drawers in a Demon House knocking people out left and right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:13:30-08:00","id":10584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=10579#post10579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, those are really clever. I love the idea of doors or drawers in a Demon House knocking people out left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept, though punking Rank 5 Angels with irresistible powers is a bit much. (shifting a number of these to Contested pretty much solves the problem, while retaining the creativity)<br /> <br /> Regardless Embeds and Exploits ripe for creative combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-14-2013, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:56:33-08:00","id":10639,"title":"","content":"Download Knowledge + Borrowed Expertise: your Ring is going to love you (especially if the duration of the latter, and not the former, is used). Free skill boosts!<br /> <br /> Solitary Confinement: use it on yourself, and you get the next best thing when you don't have access to your Bolthole with Trap Door. Unless the effects are the same as a Dramatic Failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T06:58:28-08:00","id":11245,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how 'clever' it is, but it seems to be that false-bottomed briefcases become even more useful with In My Pocket<br /> <br /> Also, could you use &quot;Everybody Knows&quot; to spread a GOOD rumour about someone? If so, then you could have one Cover spread a rumour that benefits another Cover","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:02:29-08:00","id":11246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11245#post11245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how 'clever' it is, but it seems to be that false-bottomed briefcases become even more useful with In My Pocket<br /> <br /> Also, could you use &quot;Everybody Knows&quot; to spread a GOOD rumour about someone? If so, then you could have one Cover spread a rumour that benefits another Cover</div> </div> </div> </div>Occured to me also. Pretty good for helping mortals, too.<br /> <br /> ... oh man I should see if I can fit it in if I play that defence-lawyer Guardian. Rumour: &quot;my client is innocent.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:15:30-08:00","id":11254,"title":"","content":"A lot of the messenger embeds seem like they could be really good into manipulating people into signing a pact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />All who wish to exist must first accept the existence of things beyond themselves and their current awareness, only then can existence return the favour.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://webchat.sorcery.net/?channels=theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">irc.sorcery.net #theonyxpath</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/236-ina","name":"Ina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar236_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:32:12-08:00","id":11263,"title":"","content":"Sure, you could use Everybody Knows to spread a beneficial rumor. Makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:32:41-08:00","id":11264,"title":"","content":"Setting-specific, but in Seattle you could give yourself the connection to a building for using Demon House by going into one of the splinters and faking a suicide or other ghost-producing incident. Boom, the property's always been haunted. Related: need to make some good faking death powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:35:04-08:00","id":11265,"title":"","content":"Suuuuure, but doing things in a splinter doesn't always affect the dominant timeline. (That isn't to say it wouldn't work, just that I'm not going say that, for &quot;canon&quot; purposes, it would. If I were the ST, though, I'd totally allow that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:41:44-08:00","id":11271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11264#post11264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting-specific, but in Seattle you could give yourself the connection to a building for using Demon House by going into one of the splinters and faking a suicide or other ghost-producing incident. Boom, the property's always been haunted. Related: need to make some good faking death powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chunky thing - possibly an Exploit or Interlock, not sure - that works by abandoning a Cover. Spawns a corpse from the cover; you have to drop into another Cover, or are burned if you don't have one.<br /> <br /> It'd probably make the cover more 'stable' - I reckon I might not have it degrade - but the fewer points the Cover had left when you used it to fake a death, the more obvious contradictions will show up if it's investigated. For a Cover 1, there may not even be an obvious cause of death, and since you had to walk away from the scene where you left the body, there are... risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:50:18-08:00","id":11276,"title":"","content":"I'd avoid making an interlock because fake deaths are a pretty classic twist for the genre and it produces more cool story (and paranoia) if it's not just available to a few demons with related ciphers. That said, if it's rare, that can make it a good signature move for a player character or significant NPC. So you could go either way with it. A less permenant maneuver that works similar to Alibi could be useful for short-term deception, though it'd be compromising. Another path - more of an exploit thing - is to just be able to sculpt or summon convincing fake corpses, not just of your cover(s).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:37:16-08:00","id":11358,"title":"","content":"An Alibi-like Embed of &quot;create temporary fake corpse&quot; would also be a perfect prerequisite for a &quot;dump Cover as corpse&quot; Exploit.<br /> <br /> Doing it as an Exploit does mess with a few mechanics - it jumps straight past the Compromise roll to &quot;you just lose that cover,&quot; though if you felt it was appropriate (this does seem... rather cruel, though) you could make a Compromise roll for the cover you switch to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T22:25:21-08:00","id":11898,"title":"","content":"A lot of Embeds and Exploits seem to have effects upon Dramatic Failure that...actually aren't all that painful. I mean, sure, they're either the exact opposite of what the power is &quot;supposed&quot; to do or an extremely volatile, uncontrolled overcharging, so if you actually flub your roll it's probably not going to be pretty. But, you know...you can choose to dramatically fail a roll. Including power activation rolls. Including those for powers that have suspiciously useful Dramatic Failure results. It's like getting two Embeds for the price of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T22:55:15-08:00","id":11909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11898#post11898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Embeds and Exploits seem to have effects upon Dramatic Failure that...actually aren't all that painful. I mean, sure, they're either the exact opposite of what the power is &quot;supposed&quot; to do or an extremely volatile, uncontrolled overcharging, so if you actually flub your roll it's probably not going to be pretty. But, you know...you can choose to dramatically fail a roll. Including power activation rolls. Including those for powers that have suspiciously useful Dramatic Failure results. It's like getting two Embeds for the price of one.</div> </div> </div> </div> No storyteller should allow this. Some embeds have absurdly broken powers if allowed to deliberately fail. Plus it's kinda against the spirit of the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T01:27:09-08:00","id":11955,"title":"","content":"Here's another few that just bubbled to mind:<br /> <br /> Marco Polo + Play On Words: Mumble half a song or idiom, force the target to finish it. Use Play On Words to bring about negative repercussions based on what was said. It can be tricky to use, but with the sheer number of idioms and popular song lyrics a demon can pretty much do anything. Bonus, it's all reflexive.<br /> <br /> Shift Consequence + basically anything: Assuming Shift Consequence can move magical consequences it can basically shuffle around any positive or negative effect. Angel did you five damage? Nope, did himself five damage. Angel heal himself? Nope, he healed your ally. You bribed the janitor and opened all his Doors? Nope, you bribed the CEO and opened all <b>his </b>doors. The list goes on and on, it's basically infinite. Though I must assume death cannot be shifted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T04:40:29-08:00","id":11998,"title":"","content":"I've just encountered an intellectual dilemma.<br /> What happens when someone tells a Demon to go to Hell, and they use Play On Words?<br /> (By default, I'd say bad things, that's what happens.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T07:53:50-08:00","id":12070,"title":"","content":"They get to ask their next Cipher Question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:28:56-08:00","id":13483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11998#post11998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just encountered an intellectual dilemma.<br /> What happens when someone tells a Demon to go to Hell, and they use Play On Words?<br /> (By default, I'd say bad things, that's what happens.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They wind up in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell,_Michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Michigan</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:15:17-08:00","id":13573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=13483#post13483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wind up in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell,_Michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Michigan</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, bad things happen, that's exactly what I said.<br /> (Apologies to all inhabitants of Hell, Michigan. At least, it's not New Jersey!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:02:45-08:00","id":13642,"title":"","content":"No, New Jersey is where Saboteurs go when they want to destroy the God-Machine through re-joining it. (couldn't help myself)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:58:15-08:00","id":13897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11998#post11998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just encountered an intellectual dilemma.<br /> What happens when someone tells a Demon to go to Hell, and they use Play On Words?<br /> (By default, I'd say bad things, that's what happens.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal demons. Infernal demons everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T05:43:37-08:00","id":13950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11898#post11898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Embeds and Exploits seem to have effects upon Dramatic Failure that...actually aren't all that painful. I mean, sure, they're either the exact opposite of what the power is &quot;supposed&quot; to do or an extremely volatile, uncontrolled overcharging, so if you actually flub your roll it's probably not going to be pretty. But, you know...you can choose to dramatically fail a roll. Including power activation rolls. Including those for powers that have suspiciously useful Dramatic Failure results. It's like getting two Embeds for the price of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can choose to dramatically fail a roll <i>if you failed the roll to begin with</i>. But if you're using the power, my assumption as ST is that you're trying to do what the Embed actually does. Want to do the dramatic failure effect more consistently? Fine, teach yourself to do it (that is, make up a new Embed or Exploit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T09:57:12-08:00","id":14135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=13950#post13950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can choose to dramatically fail a roll <i>if you failed the roll to begin with</i>. But if you're using the power, my assumption as ST is that you're trying to do what the Embed actually does. Want to do the dramatic failure effect more consistently? Fine, teach yourself to do it (that is, make up a new Embed or Exploit).</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of idle curiosity, is this part of why Embeds don't use untrained Skill penalties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T15:01:45-08:00","id":14314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=14135#post14135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a point of idle curiosity, is this part of why Embeds don't use untrained Skill penalties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I just don't like applying untrained penalties to supernatural powers, although strictly speaking it might make more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:28:30-08:00","id":14396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=11955#post11955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another few that just bubbled to mind:<br /> <br /> Marco Polo + Play On Words: Mumble half a song or idiom, force the target to finish it. Use Play On Words to bring about negative repercussions based on what was said. It can be tricky to use, but with the sheer number of idioms and popular song lyrics a demon can pretty much do anything. Bonus, it's all reflexive.<br /> <br /> Shift Consequence + basically anything: Assuming Shift Consequence can move magical consequences it can basically shuffle around any positive or negative effect. Angel did you five damage? Nope, did himself five damage. Angel heal himself? Nope, he healed your ally. You bribed the janitor and opened all his Doors? Nope, you bribed the CEO and opened all <b>his </b>doors. The list goes on and on, it's basically infinite. Though I must assume death cannot be shifted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish the ability work would like Shield of mars (I believe) where the person still has to roll rather than it being automatic rather than deferring it wholesale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T18:13:14-08:00","id":14419,"title":"","content":"Use it too much and you risk a compromise, and I think there's a matter of line of sight. Still useful, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:06:36-08:00","id":14978,"title":"","content":"Write the Contracts using Special Message. Now all your contracts are only visible to the signatories, and in unassuming pizza hut flyers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T02:40:30-08:00","id":15271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=14419#post14419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use it too much and you risk a compromise, and I think there's a matter of line of sight. Still useful, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think being able to pass one the Consequence of being DEAD on to an angel after you've either killed a small creature or at the worse extent a human in the back of the head is rather dumb. The rules though allow you to pass on status such as a fatal gunshot while ignoring all of said being or any supernatural being's innate toughness/fortitude or mystical defenses. All it takes is one use and dealing with compromise or dealing with a live angel are two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T04:30:47-07:00","id":128140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=15271#post15271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think being able to pass one the Consequence of being DEAD on to an angel after you've either killed a small creature or at the worse extent a human in the back of the head is rather dumb. The rules though allow you to pass on status such as a fatal gunshot while ignoring all of said being or any supernatural being's innate toughness/fortitude or mystical defenses. All it takes is one use and dealing with compromise or dealing with a live angel are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the God Machine goes &quot;... Wait a minute. My agent died from nothing. What's going on here?&quot; And the next thing the character notices is that his cover is unraveling on it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T13:23:40-07:00","id":129223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=15271#post15271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think being able to pass one the Consequence of being DEAD on to an angel after you've either killed a small creature or at the worse extent a human in the back of the head is rather dumb. The rules though allow you to pass on status such as a fatal gunshot while ignoring all of said being or any supernatural being's innate toughness/fortitude or mystical defenses. All it takes is one use and dealing with compromise or dealing with a live angel are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd rule it as damage. It's not really I shot and killed the squirrel and now you're dead, it's now I shot you instead of the squirrel. Please deal with the four lethal damage I dealt to that size one, stamina one creature. Oh, you're a vampire? I shot you so it's four bashing instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2037-iceix","name":"IceIX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:20:05-07:00","id":176228,"title":"","content":"At the risk of seeming like... conceited or something, here's one I just thought of using the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=175807#post175807\">Backdoor Embed</a> that I just revised.<br /> <br /> People are chasing you, so you activate Backdoor on a door at the end of the hall, then make it seem like you ran through. Pick a destination that's inconvenient and have them run through. Then sever the connection. Guards dispatched! Well, dispatched to... elsewhere. Of your choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:52:31-07:00","id":176732,"title":"","content":"This one takes a little bit of prep work but if you have an escape route set up that uses parkour (say, ramps on the roofs of building to leap across alleyways) Tools into Tools can allow the Demon to make that course, while giving pursuers a far smaller dice pool.<br /> <br /> Installing Tools into Toys in your doors can make your entrance ways impassable to picks and crowbars.<br /> <br /> And with the release of Heirs to Hell, there is any number of embeds that a conscientious demonic parent might use for protecting their child, Tag and Release is obvious, but Embeds like Social Dynamics and Special Someone might be used to vet a child's friends and teachers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T05:28:44-07:00","id":178823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=176228#post176228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of seeming like... conceited or something, here's one I just thought of using the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9785-building-an-embed?p=175807#post175807\">Backdoor Embed</a> that I just revised.<br /> <br /> People are chasing you, so you activate Backdoor on a door at the end of the hall, then make it seem like you ran through. Pick a destination that's inconvenient and have them run through. Then sever the connection. Guards dispatched! Well, dispatched to... elsewhere. Of your choosing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats kinda how my destroyer angel escaped his fall. Hunter Angel in pursuit, easy access &amp; cover linked bolt hole, teleported out as soon as the Angel stepped in, assumed demonic form, no more angel. Still don't know what happened to that poor chap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T06:17:29-07:00","id":184746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheFrigidMidget</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10053-creative-uses-for-embeds-exploits?p=178823#post178823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats kinda how my destroyer angel escaped his fall. Hunter Angel in pursuit, easy access &amp; cover linked bolt hole, teleported out as soon as the Angel stepped in, assumed demonic form, no more angel. Still don't know what happened to that poor chap.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lost_Room\" target=\"_blank\">The Lost Room</a>, twiddling his tumbs :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T03:31:35-07:00","id":186155,"title":"","content":"Hellfire exploit + sword gadget installation = lightsaber?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T08:12:24-07:00","id":187075,"title":"","content":"Two Places At Once + Alibi: Theoretically, you could be in *three* places at once. Or, take meaningful action in two separate places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T09:20:59-07:00","id":187150,"title":"","content":"Limited value of meaningful-the Cover runs on automatic and lives life as simply as it possibly can.<br /> <br /> Alibi+Terrible Avatar+Two Places At Once, though......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:52:54-07:00","id":216226,"title":"","content":"Take <b>Persistent Legend</b>, with a legend roll at the -400 with all the merits and skills you could possibly justify to yourself with your cover having. Add <b>Victory at Any Price</b> and watch yourself getting 1 success there (assuming you don't dramatically fail the Legend roll in the first place). Now you have a -perfect- cover in terms of traits.<br /> <br /> Example of what a 20 years in the force Vice Detective got with it:<br /> <br /> *Investigation 4 (Small Details)<br /> Academics 2<br /> Politics 2<br /> *Streetwise 3 (Service Procurement)<br /> Drive 3<br /> Brawl 3 <br /> *Firearms 4 (Sidearm)<br /> Weaponry 2<br /> Medicine 1 <br /> Computer 1<br /> <br /> Status 3 (SPD; Senior Detective) <br /> Allies 3 (IA) <br /> Professional Training 5 (Empathy, Investigation, Firearms)<br /> Contacts (Confidential Informants, First Responders) <br /> Good Time Management 1 <br /> Patient 1 <br /> Trained Observer 3 <br /> Tolerance for Biology 1 <br /> Fleet of Foot 3 <br /> Crack Driver 3 <br /> Quick Draw 1 (Sidearm) <br /> Fast-Talking 5 <br /> Fixer 2 <br /> Resources 3 <br /> Pusher 1 <br /> Chokehold 2 <br /> Close Quarters Combat Style 5 <br /> Police Tactics Combat Style 3 <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 08-01-2014, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 20